      "message": "The flag is the right fix for the reported bug. One channel from the same root cause is left open (pre-existing, not this patch\u0027s doing): `markup\u003dTrue` still applies to table cell strings, so free-text cells lose bracket sequences. Verified with rich 14.3.2 and `emoji\u003dFalse`:\n\n    \"rack [h01] u01\"            -\u003e \"rack  u01\"        # [h01] eaten entirely\n    \"vsan[b]x\"                  -\u003e \"vsanx\"\n    \"alloc [red]urgent[/red]\"   -\u003e \"alloc urgent\"\n    \"env [DEV] tier-1\"          -\u003e unchanged (unknown tag kept)\n\nReachable through the free-text Description columns of `--summary --detail` (cli.py:2430) and the Detailed Report (reports.py:242), so the issue\u0027s root-cause point 1 (\"markup\u003dTrue ... the MAC text is never escaped\") is only half-addressed by this patch.\n\nIf that is ever closed, the route that handles both properties is per-cell `Text(value)` in `add_row` for data columns -- `Text` is a renderable, so markup and emoji parsing are both skipped (verified: `Text(\"04:32:01:ab:62:f1\")` and `Text(\"rack [h01] u01\")` render verbatim). That would also have made console-level `emoji\u003dFalse` redundant for tables, at the cost of touching every `add_row`.\n\nSuggest a separate follow-up issue for the markup half rather than growing this patch; #754 as titled is fixed by PS1 as-is.\n",
